    {
      "n": 1,
      "signpost": null,
      "definition": "a form of a verb, such as **broken** or **breaking**, that is used to make some verb forms and can also be used like an adjective",
      "explanation": "English has two. The present participle ends in **-ing** (*walking*, *eating*). The past participle usually ends in **-ed** (*walked*), but many common verbs have a form of their own (*eaten*, *gone*); it follows **have** (*has eaten*) and is used in the passive (*was eaten*).",
      "grammar": {
        "countability": "countable",
        "transitivity": null,
